# PortLess — production readiness to-do

Everything that has to be true before PortLess moves real buyer and supplier money, plus the
features that would raise profit per deal. Written 2026-11-13 from the code on `main`
(backend `df50ecc`, UI `f229046`), the production readiness gate, the test catalogue and the
end-to-end automation runs.

**Priority** — **P0**: blocks the first real trade (money, law or data can be lost or wrong).
**P1**: needed before running more than a handful of deals a month. **P2**: improvement.
**Owner** — (Eng) engineering · (Ops) operations / trade desk · (Legal) lawyer or chartered
accountant · (Biz) founder / business · (QA) quality.

---

**Layout** — the owner's accounts and keys are in their own section (right after the go-live blockers) so they can be done in parallel. The rest is grouped by priority first (P0, then P1, then P2), then by area. Area numbers (1.1, 3.3, 5.5 …) are kept in every priority so a reference such as "see 3.3" points to the same area wherever its items sit. Background for an area is in the appendix at the end.

---

## Where things stand today

- [ ] **P0 (Eng/Ops)** Production readiness gate (`ENV_PROFILE=production`, `GET /health/readiness`): **12 fail, 5 warn, 19 ok**. Production refuses to boot until every fail is fixed — section 1 lists each one.
- Backend tests: 4574 passed, 1 skipped. Coverage 95.46 % line + branch (measured 2026-11-09, before the latest features — re-measure).
- End-to-end automation: TC-E2E-000 / UC-15 (scan opportunity → PAID on every simulator) passes 56/56 checks; UC-01 passes 35/35. UC-02 … UC-14 were not re-run after the latest changes.
- Gherkin catalogue: 589 cases. **81 are browser-only and nothing drives the console. 34 backend cases still have unautomated steps — 24 of them P0.** 95 production-risk cases (TC-RSK, 52 P0) were added on 2026-11-13 and none is automated yet; 32 new browser cases (TC-WEB) are in `docs/testing/BROWSER_SCENARIOS.md` (section 6).
- UI repo: type-check passes; **no tests of any kind, no CI**.
- Neither repo has CI. Nothing runs the test suites automatically on a push to `main`.

---

## Go-live blockers — the short list

Everything here is P0; the areas are named in brackets.

- [ ] Real credentials for every provider in the money path, each verified against the provider's own sandbox first (section 1, section 2).
- [ ] Legal set-up of the exporter, the escrow route and the supplier payment route signed off by a lawyer / CA (section 3).
- [ ] The company exists and is registered: incorporated, PAN / TAN, GSTIN, IEC, LUT, AD code, RCMC for each product, AD-bank current + EEFC account, website and e-mail on its own domain (section 14).
- [ ] Decide how Indian suppliers are paid (INR in India vs Payoneer USD) — today's design may not be legal for a domestic purchase (section 3.3).
- [ ] Money writes made atomic and reconciled daily against the provider statements (section 4).
- [ ] PI acceptance that names a different price must not pass as an acceptance (section 5.1).
- [ ] Local suppliers can be added by hand and start the workflow (section 5.5).
- [ ] Durable event bus, backups, monitoring, alerting and single-instance background watchers (section 7).
- [ ] CI on both repos; the 24 P0 catalogue cases automated; UC-01 … UC-15 green on a nightly run (section 6).
- [ ] One pilot trade with a small, real lot, a known buyer and a known supplier, before opening the funnel (section 6.7).
- [ ] Test strategy in place: unit, integration, sanity / smoke and regression suites defined, in CI and green (6.9 – 6.13).
- [ ] Buyer / supplier checks actually answer: Apify screening live, GSTN path fixed, and quote intake no longer passes an unchecked supplier as verified (section 12).

---

## Owner's parallel track — accounts, API keys and tokens to hand over

Things only the founder can do: open the accounts, accept the terms, pass the provider's KYC / KYB and copy the keys. Work through this list while engineering works on the rest. Put each value in the backend's environment (local `.env`, and the hosting platform's environment variables for the deployed backend). **Never paste a key into chat, an e-mail or a commit.** After setting a group, run `GET /health/readiness` (System Health page) and `python scripts/check_trade_api_connections.py`, then tick the box. The section numbers in brackets point to the detailed item.

### A. Can be done now (no company registration needed)
- [ ] **auth-service app account** — ask the RouteToRich auth-service admin for PortLess's account id → `PORTLESS_ACCOUNT_ID`; set `AUTH_GATEWAY_URL`, `FRONTEND_URL` and the staff allowlist `AUTH_PORTLESS_EMAILS` (1.5, 8).
- [ ] **LLM gateway service account** — `LLM_GATEWAY_URL`, `LLM_GATEWAY_EMAIL`, `LLM_GATEWAY_PASSWORD`, `LLM_GATEWAY_ACCOUNT_ID` (or a pre-minted `LLM_GATEWAY_TOKEN`) on the deployed backend; set a monthly cost budget (2.7).
- [ ] **MongoDB Atlas** — production cluster, `MONGO_URI` + `MONGO_DB_NAME`; turn on continuous backup (7).
- [ ] **Synadia Cloud (NATS)** — create the account, download the user `.creds` file → `NATS_CREDS_FILE` (1.5).
- [ ] **Google Drive** — OAuth "Desktop app" client in console.cloud.google.com → `GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID` / `_CLIENT_SECRET`; run `python scripts/google_drive_authorize.py` once → `GOOGLE_DRIVE_REFRESH_TOKEN` (1.4).
- [ ] **Apify** — API token from console.apify.com (Settings → Integrations) → `APIFY_TOKEN`; set `APIFY_MAX_RUNS_PER_DAY`; decide the plan upgrade so Store actors (buyer finders, carrier tracking) run (2.6, 12).
- [ ] **Telegram alerts** — create a bot with @BotFather → `HITL_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`; the operators' group chat id → `HITL_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID`; `DIGEST_EMAIL_TO` (1.5).
- [ ] **Tavily** — API key → `TAVILY_API_KEY` (market check, live USD/INR rate) (2.6, 5.4).
- [ ] **UN Comtrade** — subscription key from comtradedeveloper.un.org → `COMTRADE_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY` (2.6).
- [ ] **Free trade-data keys you want** — `MACMAP_API_KEY`, `CENSUS_API_KEY` (optional) (2.6).
- [ ] **Signing secrets** — generate random strings (e.g. `python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"`) for `ESCROW_PROOF_LINK_SECRET` and `HITL_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`; set `PORTLESS_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` to the backend's public HTTPS address (1.1).
- [ ] **Controls** — choose `FOUR_EYES_THRESHOLD_USD` (suggested 25000) and keep `AUTONOMY_MONEY_CEILING=L1` (1.1).

### B. Needs the company's domain and mailbox (14.4)
- [ ] **Outbound mail** — trade-desk mailbox on the company domain: `GMAIL_SENDER_ADDRESS` + `GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD` (Google Workspace app password) or a transactional provider; `PORTLESS_EMAIL_DOMAIN` with SPF, DKIM and DMARC records at the DNS host (1.3).
- [ ] **Inbound mail** — `IMAP_USER` / `IMAP_PASSWORD`, or SendGrid Inbound Parse (`SENDGRID_WEBHOOK_PUBLIC_KEY`) / Mailgun routes (`MAILGUN_SIGNING_KEY`) (1.3).
- [ ] **Company profile in e-mails** — `PORTLESS_LEGAL_NAME`, `PORTLESS_BRAND_NAME`, `PORTLESS_SENDER_NAME` / `_TITLE`, `PORTLESS_WEBSITE`, `PORTLESS_PHONE`, `PORTLESS_CONTACT_EMAIL` (1.4).

### C. Needs the registered company (section 14 first)
- [ ] **Exporter facts on every document** — `PORTLESS_ADDRESS`, `PORTLESS_IEC`, `PORTLESS_GSTIN`, `PORTLESS_PAN`, `PORTLESS_LUT_ARN`, `PORTLESS_AD_CODE`, `PORTLESS_SIGNATORY_NAME` / `_TITLE`, `DEALMAKER_PORTLESS_ENTITY_IEC` / `_GSTIN`, `PORTLESS_CONTRACT_LAW` (governing law + arbitration seat), `PORTLESS_MARINE_POLICY` (open marine policy number) (1.4).
- [ ] **API Setu (GSTN / MCA / Udyam)** — subscribe on apisetu.gov.in (GSTN Tax Payer product) → `API_SETU_KEY`; tell engineering the real GSTN path (12).
- [ ] **Tazapay** — business account + KYB; from the dashboard: `TAZAPAY_API_KEY`, `TAZAPAY_API_SECRET`, `TAZAPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`; start with `TAZAPAY_ENV=sandbox`, switch to `production` after the sandbox run; ask Tazapay for the release event names and the 4-stage payout (1.1, 2.1).
- [ ] **Escrow.com** — business account; `ESCROW_COM_API_KEY`, `ESCROW_COM_EMAIL`, `ESCROW_COM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (any random string; it goes into the webhook URL); or drop `escrow_com` from `ESCROW_PROVIDERS_ENABLED` until it is live (1.1, 2.2).
- [ ] **QIMA** — client account + Public API access: `QIMA_API_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `QIMA_ACCOUNT`, `QIMA_PASSWORD`; product tree ids per product line → `QIMA_PRODUCT_CATEGORY_ID` / `_FAMILY_ID` / `_TYPE_ID`; ask QIMA for the PEO service type → `QIMA_SERVICE_TYPE_PEO` (1.2, 2.4).
- [ ] **Maersk** — customer account + developer.maersk.com app: `MAERSK_CONSUMER_KEY`, `MAERSK_CLIENT_SECRET`, `MAERSK_CUSTOMER_CODE`, `MAERSK_SERVICE_CONTRACT`, `MAERSK_CARRIER_SERVICE_CODE` (your lane's service), `MAERSK_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (1.2, 2.3).
- [ ] **Freight forwarder (quotes, non-Maersk lanes)** — `COGOPORT_API_KEY` + `COGOPORT_WEBHOOK_SECRET` or `FREIGHTOS_API_KEY` + `FREIGHTOS_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (1.2).
- [ ] **ICEGATE** — API access (direct, aggregator or via the CHA) → `ICEGATE_API_KEY`; or confirm the CHA files manually (1.2, 5.2).
- [ ] **Supplier payouts** — only after decision 3.3: `PAYONEER_CLIENT_ID`, `PAYONEER_CLIENT_SECRET`, `PAYONEER_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (or the INR bank / gateway credentials chosen instead) (1.1, 3.3).
- [ ] **Optional sources** — `VOLZA_API_KEY`, `INDIAMART_API_KEY` / `INDIAMART_MOBILE`, `ALIBABA_APP_KEY` / `_APP_SECRET`; `SGS_BOOKING_EMAIL` / `BUREAU_VERITAS_BOOKING_EMAIL` if those inspectors will be offered (1.2, 2.6).

### D. After the keys are in
- [ ] Load the real product lines and corridors on the Catalogue page (`PUT /trade-min/catalogue`) (1.5).
- [ ] Tell engineering which groups are set, so each provider's sandbox run (6.3) can start; readiness should show no `fail` before `ENV_PROFILE=production`.

