## Decisions needed

Sorted by priority; each names the area it belongs to.

- [ ] **P0** How Indian suppliers are paid and in which currency the PO is written (3.3).
- [ ] **P0** Whether the CHA files customs manually until ICEGATE works (1.2, 5.2).
- [ ] **P0** Exposure limits and four-eyes threshold (1.1, 4).
- [ ] **P0** Who holds the money-approver role (4, 8).
- [ ] **P0** For a manually added supplier whose price is already known: skip the RFQ e-mail and record the price, or still send the RFQ so the supplier commits in writing (5.5). **Recommendation:** allow both, default to recording the phone price — the firm order request before the PI already makes the supplier confirm in writing, so the RFQ adds little. To be built later.
- [ ] **P1** Real order of carrier booking vs stuffing (2.3).
- [ ] **P1** Which inspectors to offer beyond QIMA (1.2).
- [ ] **P1** Apify plan upgrade vs other data sources (2.6).
- [ ] **P1** Monolith vs microservices in production (7).
- [ ] **P1** Which buyer currencies to support and from which rate source (5.4).
- [ ] **P1** Outreach / RFQ to verified counterparties only, or also to unverified ones (today: unverified yes, failed never) (12). **Recommendation:** verified only for buyers once screening is live (cold e-mail to an unscreened company is the bigger risk); keep unverified suppliers in the RFQ because GST / IEC are verified at quote anyway.
- [ ] **P1** Source for proof that a buyer imports the product: paid bill-of-lading data (Volza / ImportGenius), Apify plan upgrade, or a new PortLess actor on public US bill-of-lading data (12).
- [ ] **P1** Firm offers before composition: may PortLess take a buyer's "yes, subject to final order confirmation" and a supplier's firm price without committing to either until the composition gate? Each side needs to know how long its offer binds. Needs a lawyer's wording (13.2, 3.6).
- [ ] **P1** Lots from more than one supplier under one contract: tell the buyer in advance ("may be supplied from more than one mill / origin, same specification") or ask each time? How many suppliers are allowed per deal (`COMPOSITION_MAX_SUPPLIERS`)? (13.3) **Recommendation:** a standard clause in the Sales Contract, at most 2 suppliers at the start, same grade only.
- [ ] **P1** One Shipping Bill for goods from several suppliers / ports, or one per port of loading — confirm with the CHA (13.4).
- [ ] **P1** Composition gate always L0, or auto-approve when the margin is above a set level and every party is verified (13.3). **Recommendation:** always L0 until 20 compositions are resolved (`outcomes.py` calibration).
- [ ] **P2** Buyers & Suppliers page default: all companies (today) or verified only like the radar (12).

---
- [ ] **P0** Legal form of the company (private limited, LLP or proprietorship) and the state of the registered office — every registration depends on it (14.1). **Recommendation:** private limited.
- [ ] **P0** Which AD Category-I bank (forex desk, export credit, EDPMS support, charges) (14.3).
- [ ] **P1** Which products to register for first (decides the RCMC: Spices Board, APEDA, FIEO) (14.2).

## Done in the latest rounds (for reference)

- Full-flow journey TC-E2E-000 / UC-15 on every simulator; `@journey:` link between Gherkin and journeys.
- Fixed: RFQ to scan-found suppliers, SDF / Shipping Bill on CIF deals, nameless e-mailed quotes, QIMA booking without a supplier address, Tazapay proof links in automation.
- Supplier facility address asked, read from e-mails and required before the inspection (`QC_FACILITY_ADDRESS_REQUIRED`).
- Prices to Indian suppliers in INR with the USD contract price and rate; quotations mirrored in their own currency.
- Confirming a match closes the deal's other proposals.
- Buyer / supplier check at scan time (12): the top buyers and suppliers of every opportunity are screened (sanctions, e-mail, GST / IEC) before the radar shows them; the radar shows verified ones by default ("Verified only / All" toggle, hidden counts), the directory filters by result and can check one company now, a failed counterparty never seeds outreach or a supplier party, and a deal from an opportunity no longer records an unchecked supplier as verified.
- Pre-deal rescore (12): the radar's Rescore / Start prospect fills the best pairs' gaps without contacting anyone (counterparty check, supplier address / GSTIN from its website, plant-to-port distance, an estimated supplier price labelled as an estimate), scores them again and shows before → after; a web-search buyer's product fit is no longer overstated as "same subheading".
- Readiness check `counterparty_validation` (12): fails in production (warns elsewhere) when `TRADE_MIN_VALIDATION_ENABLED=false` or the screening actor has no `APIFY_TOKEN`, so the radar's "Verified only" view can no longer be silently empty.

